ned on a room box</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>U3</b> A box that starts with a room number (e.g. 'bed 415…') shows a room chip, and the picker suggests that room's patient. The physician still taps to assign; nothing auto-assigns. (UAT TC-04; TFA-92582 AC 4; TFA-92582 step 4; TFA-92583 AC 3)</li><li><b>U6</b> No auto-assignment anywhere: the app never splits one dictation across patients, never routes by name or room, and never merges boxes. There is no AI routing. (UAT TC-04; TFA-92582 AC 2; TFA-92583 AC 2)</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>Equivalence classes (equivalence) — Check the same rule again with another class of input (Hospital / Nursing Home, other data); every class has to be right.</p><p><b>Given </b>QA Hosp Patel in room 415, QA Hosp Ortiz in room 416</p><p><b>When </b>Type into one box, replacing the text each time: 'bed 415 seen at 7, comfortable.' (then open Assign to patient on it and close the picker), 'Room 415: pain 3/10, on oral analgesia.', 'Rm. #415 — dressing changed.', '415 — afebrile, eating breakfast.', 'Looks better this morning, lungs clear.', 'QA Hosp Ortiz looks be …</p><p><b>Then </b>Each of the four room forms shows the chip and suggests Patel; the picker opened on the room box lists Patel (where he sits is recorded for Q1); the no-room text and the name-only text show no chip and no suggestion, and the name never routes the box to Ortiz; no text reaches either chart without a tap</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>oracle.mjs: cp1 and cp3–cp5 mustContain 'Rm 415' and '415 · QA Hosp Patel', mustNotContain 'Re-assign' (U3). cp2 (picker open on the room box) mustContain 'Assign to patient', 'Search room or name', '415 · QA Hosp Patel', mustNotContain 'Re-assign'; Patel's place in the list and any mark are recorded for Q1. cp6 mustNotContain 'Rm 415' and 'Matches on your list'. …</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>dev unit U14; test method AGENT · Browser agent; lane planned in the matrix: browser 